### Article 3. Subjects of domestic violence

(1) Subjects of domestic violence are the aggressor and the victim who are members of the same family.

(2) Family members, within the meaning of this law, are:

a) in the condition of cohabitation: persons who are married, divorced, under guardianship and curatorship, in respect of whom a judicial protection measure has been instituted, relatives, their in-laws, spouses of relatives, persons in relationships similar to those between spouses (cohabitation) or between parents and children;
[Art.3 para.(2), let.a) amended by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
b) in the condition of separate residence: persons who are married, divorced, relatives, their in-laws, adopted children, persons under curatorship, in respect of whom a judicial protection measure has been instituted, persons who are or have been in relationships similar to those between spouses (cohabitation).
[Art.3 para.(2), let.b) amended by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in

force 07.09.20]

### Article 4. Legislative framework

(1) The legislation on the prevention and combating of domestic violence consists of the Constitution of the Republic of Moldova, this law, other normative acts, and international treaties to which the Republic of Moldova is a party.
(2) If an international treaty to which the Republic of Moldova is a party establishes other rules than this law, the rules of the international treaty shall apply.

### Article 5

Basic principles of prevention and combating of domestic violence The prevention and combating of domestic violence is carried out on the following principles:
a) legality;

b) equality and non-discrimination;

c) confidentiality;

d) access to justice;

e) protection and security of the victim;

f) cooperation of public administration authorities with civil society and with international organizations.

### Article 6. Scope of the law

The provisions of this law apply equally to citizens of the Republic of Moldova, foreign citizens and stateless persons residing on its territory.

## Chapter II

AUTHORITIES AND INSTITUTIONS EMPOWERED WITH FUNCTIONS OF PREVENTION AND COMBATING
OF DOMESTIC VIOLENCE

### Article 7

Authorities and institutions empowered with functions of prevention and combating of domestic violence
(1) The authorities and institutions empowered with functions of prevention and combating of domestic violence are:
a) central specialized bodies of the state (, the Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection, the Ministry of Education, Culture and Research, the Ministry of Internal Affairs, the Ministry of Justice);
b) specialized authorities of the second level local public administration and deconcentrated structures: sections/directorates of social assistance and family protection;
	general directorates of education, youth and sport;
	health protection bodies;
	territorial subdivisions of the police;

c) first level local public administration;

d) centres/services for assistance and protection of victims of domestic violence and their children and centres/services for assistance and counselling for family aggressors;
e) other organizations with specialized activities in the field.

(2) The central specialized body empowered with functions of elaboration and promotion of policies for prevention and combating of domestic violence and social assistance of victims and aggressors is the Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection.
(3) Under the Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection, the Interministerial Coordinating Council in the field of prevention and combating of domestic violence is created, composed of one representative of the central authorities, according to para. (1), representatives of civil society and other interested parties. The Interministerial Coordinating Council is responsible for ensuring coordination and collaboration between ministries and other central administrative authorities with competences in the field of prevention and combating of domestic violence. The Regulation of the Interministerial Coordinating Council is approved by Government decision.
(4) The local public authority empowered with functions of implementation of policies for prevention of domestic violence and social assistance of victims and aggressors is the district section/directorate of social assistance and family protection, within which a specialist responsible for the field of prevention and combating of domestic violence is designated.
(5) The other public services at local level shall designate persons with duties regarding the prevention and combating of domestic violence, responsible for coordinating specific activities within their institution and for collaboration in carrying out joint activities at the level of the administrative territory, based on established procedures for cooperation in the prevention and combating of cases of domestic violence.

