### Article 8. Competences of central and local public administration authorities

(1) The central specialized state bodies (Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection, Ministry of Education, Culture and Research, Ministry of Internal Affairs, Ministry of Justice), within the limits of their competence:
a) ensure the development and promotion of policies for strengthening the family, preventing and combating domestic violence, providing protection and assistance to victims and aggressors;
b) coordinate the activity in the field of decentralized/deconcentrated structures;

c) ensure access to information for persons regarding the mechanism, measures for preventing and combating acts of domestic violence and contribute to updating the official web page on domestic violence by transferring information of a general nature regarding the activities carried out and projects implemented, as well as statistical data collected based on uniform indicators for all authorities, which are included in the statistical work programmes approved by the Government;
[Art.8 para.(1), let.c) amended by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in

force 07.09.20]

d) systematically collect statistical data in the field disaggregated by sex, provide support in conducting research on the phenomenon of domestic violence;
e) consolidate the capacities of human resources in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence, ensure their continuous training and professional development;
f) cooperate with non-governmental organizations, with natural and legal persons involved in activities for preventing and combating violence.
(11) The Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection, in its capacity as the central specialized state body, empowered with functions of developing and promoting policies for preventing and combating domestic violence, as well as social assistance to victims and aggressors, shall ensure:
a) the creation and maintenance of the official web page on preventing and combating domestic violence in order to provide the population with access to information about the mechanism for resolving acts of domestic violence, the infrastructure of social services for victims of domestic violence and for aggressors, as well as to the results of studies and research in the field;
b) the establishment and maintenance of a free telephone assistance service that provides counselling to callers, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, regarding the prevention of domestic violence and regarding the services available to subjects of domestic violence. The service is anonymous and confidential;
c) the organization, jointly with development partners, of studies and information campaigns for preventing and combating domestic violence;
d) the preparation of an annual report on domestic violence and violence against women with the participation of all authorities and institutions empowered with the function of preventing and combating domestic violence. The annual report shall be submitted to the Government by 31 March and made public.
(2) Local public administration authorities:

b) form multidisciplinary teams in the field;

c) establish and ensure, within the limits of allocated and/or available financial resources, the financing of centres/services for assistance and protection of victims of domestic violence and their children and centres/services for assistance and counselling for domestic aggressors;
c) 1 contribute to the social inclusion of victims of domestic violence by creating opportunities for retraining and/or employment in the labour market, ensure their access to social housing;
d) include in local development programmes the issue of preventing and combating domestic violence; plan the organization of studies and information campaigns to combat domestic violence, to support social services and other measures to assist victims of domestic violence, collaborate in implementing the system for recording cases of domestic violence;
e) develop social partnerships with non-governmental organizations, including foundations, trade unions, employers' organizations, religious worship organizations, international bodies that contribute

to preventing and combating domestic violence;

(21) The local guardianship authority:

a) ensures initial assessment and implementation of urgent measures to protect children in cases of domestic violence where imminent danger to the child's life and health is found;
b) ensures, at local level, confidential mechanisms for reporting cases of domestic violence;
c) collaborates with territorial guardianship authorities in order to ensure the protection of child victims of domestic violence.
(3) The social assistance and family protection sections/directorates, through the service responsible for the field of preventing and combating domestic violence:
[Art.8 para.(3) amended by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
a) cooperate with police bodies in the activity of identifying persons predisposed to committing acts of domestic violence;
b) update the database, at territorial level, concerning the phenomenon of domestic violence;

c) place, as appropriate, the victim in the rehabilitation centre, providing them with appropriate assistance;

d) in order to eliminate the consequences of acts of domestic violence, redirect the case to specialists from assistance and protection centres/services;
e) facilitate, at the request of law enforcement bodies, the aggressor's access to rehabilitation programmes;
f) apply, under the conditions of the law, with a request for the application of protection measures; participate as an interested person in proceedings for requesting protection measures for the victim subjected to domestic violence; submit, at the request of the court, informative materials characterizing the family concerned and the alleged aggressor, as well as other information that the court considers necessary when examining the case; contribute, under the conditions of the law, to the execution of the measures established in the protection order; carry out other activities to defend the rights and legitimate interests of victims, including minor victims;
[Art.8 para.(3), let.f) as worded by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
g) implement, jointly with other empowered authorities and in collaboration with non-governmental organizations in the field, information programmes to prevent domestic violence;
h) determine the need to create centres/services for assistance and protection of victims of domestic violence and their children and centres/services for assistance and counselling of domestic aggressors, ensuring their methodological and informational support;
i) monitor and coordinate the professional activities of social workers within town halls for preventing domestic violence, supporting/counselling victims and resocializing aggressors;

j) submit to the Ministry of Health, Labour and Social Protection semi-annual reports on the activities carried out in the territory by sections/directorates, social workers according to established partnerships;
k) monitor victims and provide them with assistance after they have left rehabilitation centres.

(4) The general directorates of education, youth and sport:

a) ensure the information and training of teaching staff in order to qualify acts of domestic violence, apply methods and means of preventing such acts and notify empowered authorities;
b) implement, jointly with other empowered authorities and in collaboration with non-governmental organizations in the field, educational programmes for parents and children to prevent and combat domestic violence;
c) ensure the conduct of counselling activities for the psychological and psychosocial rehabilitation of child victims of domestic violence;
d) communicate to empowered authorities, through teaching staff, immediately and mandatorily notifying the guardianship authority and the police, cases of domestic violence, including cases of domestic violence against children.
(5) Medical institutions of all types and levels:

a) organize information campaigns;

b) communicate to the police and the guardianship authority, through medical staff, cases of domestic violence;
c) ensure counselling and medical assistance to victims;

c1) resolve, within the limits of competence, the victim's request for forensic medical examination of the severity of bodily injury or harm to health;
d) initiate and implement programmes and services addressed to aggressors; ensure the implementation of detoxification, de-addiction, psychotherapeutic treatment programmes, as appropriate, with expenses borne by the abuser or, as appropriate, from compulsory health insurance funds;
e) initiate sustainable partnerships with all programmes concerning the health of mother and child;
f) conclude contracts for the provision of medical services with centres/services for the rehabilitation of victims and aggressors.
(6) Police bodies, at the level of specialized structure:

a) identify, register and report cases of domestic violence;

b) ensure nominal records of aggressors;

c) notify the local guardianship authority about each case of domestic violence involving a child victim/witness;

[Art.8 para.(6), let.c) as worded by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
d) examine requests and notifications received from citizens, medical institutions, forensic medical centres and other institutions regarding family conflicts, acts of violence, death threats or the existence of an imminent danger of their occurrence;
e) visit families whose members are registered, carry out work to prevent the repeated commission of acts of domestic violence;
f) issue an emergency restraining order against the aggressor if, from the circumstances established at the scene, as a result of risk assessment, there is a reasonable suspicion that acts of domestic violence have been committed and/or an imminent danger of repetition/commission of violent actions persists;
g) apply to judicial authorities to obtain a protection order in a crisis situation based on the application submitted by the victim or the case notification; ensure supervision of the execution of the protection order;
h) in the event of the commission of an act of domestic violence, explain to the victim their rights, and at their request, provide assistance for them to be placed in a rehabilitation centre;
i) inform the victim about their right to benefit from free legal assistance;

k) maintain public order and security in the vicinity of centres/services for assistance and protection of victims of domestic violence and their children, under the conditions of the law;
l) monitor and investigate, jointly with social workers, cases of domestic violence in the served territory, update the database with information in the field;
m) cooperate with empowered authorities in the field, with civil society in order to prevent and combat domestic violence.
(7) The authorities mentioned in art. 7 para. (4) and para. (5):

a) identify potential families affected by violence and ensure the recording of cases of domestic violence in the locality;
b) identify crisis situations and refer victims of domestic violence to specialized services;
c) ensure the exchange of information with other persons involved in examining the case;

d) inform the service responsible for the field of preventing and combating domestic violence about the case found and the measures taken, and about cases of violence in families with children also inform the local guardianship authority;
[Art.8 para.(7), let.d) as worded by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
e) provide police bodies with the necessary support in the process of criminal prosecution of cases of domestic violence;
f) provide victims and aggressors with information services regarding their rights and responsibilities

, bodies empowered with competences in the field, the infrastructure of social services;

g) provide, upon request, the results of findings on cases of domestic violence to law enforcement bodies, the victim, the aggressor or their representatives;
h) carry out other actions, according to competence, in order to prevent and combat acts of violence, ensure effective protection of victims of domestic violence, resocialize aggressors.
(8) In order to ensure a systemic approach to the protection and assistance of subjects of domestic violence, the conduct of joint activities for preventing and combating domestic violence, including the activities mentioned in para. (7), empowered specialists are designated, by order of the head, to the territorial multidisciplinary team.
(9) The member of the territorial multidisciplinary team:

a) is responsible for the results of the work performed;

b) ensures the confidentiality of information regarding the identity and private life of the victim;

c) collaborates effectively with other team members;

d) participates in team meetings;

e) fulfils tasks within the time limits provided by legislation.

