### Article 121. Issuance of the emergency restraining order

(1) In case of establishment at the scene, as a result of risk assessment, of circumstances from which a reasonable suspicion arises that acts of domestic violence have been committed and/or an imminent danger of repetition or commission of violent actions persists, the police body is obliged to immediately order the issuance of the emergency restraining order against the aggressor to remove the crisis situation and, concurrently, undertake the necessary actions to establish the commission of the offence of domestic violence.  
(11) The police body has the right to apply one or more of the following measures against the aggressor:
a) obligation to temporarily leave the common dwelling or to stay away from the victim's dwelling;  

b) prohibition from approaching the victim, respecting the distance that would ensure the victim's security and excluding any visual contact with the victim and/or children;  
c) prohibition of any contact, including by telephone or any other means of communication, with the victim and/or children;  
d) prohibition from keeping and carrying weapons.  

[Art.121 para.(11) introduced by LP113 of 09.07.20, MO199-204/07.08.20 art.400; in force 07.09.20]
(2) The emergency restraining order is issued for a period of up to 10 days and is immediately enforced, the aggressor and the victim (in the case of children – the legal representative of the victim) being informed about the restrictions applied, the rights and obligations incumbent upon them and about the liability for non-compliance with the requirements of the restraining order.  
(3) Supervision of the fulfilment of the measures established in the emergency restraining order is exercised by the employees of the police station or police sector in the locality in the manner provided by law.  
(4) The aggressor has the right to challenge the emergency restraining order in court under the conditions of administrative litigation. The filing of the application does not suspend the effect of the restraining order.  
(5) The victim has the right, during the period of effect of the emergency restraining order, to request, under the conditions of the law, the issuance of a protection order. The effect of the emergency restraining order, in this case, is extended by operation of law and ceases upon the enforcement of the protection measures established by the court.

### Article 13. Filing of the application

(1) The application concerning the commission of acts of domestic violence is filed:

a) with the police bodies;  

b) in court;  

c) with the social assistance and family and child protection body;  

d) with the local public administration authority.  

(2) The application is filed at the place:

a) of domicile of the victim;  

b) of temporary residence of the victim if the victim has left the domicile to avoid the continuation of direct violence;  
c) of residence of the aggressor;  

d) where the victim sought assistance;  

e) where the act of violence occurred.  

(21) The application for the issuance of a protection order is filed by the victim personally or through a representative. In case of impossibility of filing the application by the victim due to health, age, other well-founded reasons, at the victim's request, the application for the issuance of a protection order may be filed, in the interests of the victim, by the police body, the social assistance body or by the prosecutor. The application for the issuance of a protection order in the interests of a child or of a person in respect of whom a judicial guardianship measure has been instituted may be filed by the local guardianship authority or by the prosecutor even in the absence of a request from the victim or the victim's legal representative.  
(3) No state fee is paid for filing in court the application for the issuance of a protection order.

### Article 14. Manner of examination of the application

(1) The application filed with the police body is examined according to the procedure provided by the legislation in force.  
(2) The application or request for the issuance of a protection order filed in court is examined according to the Code of Civil Procedure, the Code of Criminal Procedure.  
(3) The application filed with any authority empowered with functions of prevention and combating of domestic violence is referred according to competence within one working day.
